cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software
  (this record) and the preprint listed under preferred-citation. The MIT
  licence declared below covers the code, the manuscript and the documentation
  authored here; refs/ redistributes third-party material under its own
  licences (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 and CC BY 4.0) and is not covered by it -- see
  NOTICE.md.
title: >-
  Conserved CRISPR-Cas9 target sites in HSV-1: alignment-free conservation,
  multiplex escape modelling and human off-target screening
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a computational audit of multiplex CRISPR antiviral guide
  design against herpes simplex virus type 1. The pipeline retrieves every
  complete HSV-1 genome in GenBank, enumerates SpCas9 and SaCas9 target sites
  inside seven essential genes from the reference annotation, scores
  conservation by exact alignment-free substring presence, and adds four
  opt-in stages: denominator robustness, a SaCas9 head-to-head against the
  EBT-104 guide set of Amrani et al. 2024, a quantitative multiplex
  escape-probability model over a per-genome presence matrix, and an exact
  human GRCh38 off-target screen. Dependency-light pure Python; no aligner and
  no compiled tooling.
type: software

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Author identity, including the ORCID, is final (see PUBLISH.md Step 0). The
# repository URL and the Zenodo concept DOI are now filled in. The only
# placeholder left below is the bioRxiv DOI, for a preprint that is not yet
# posted; it must NOT be invented. See PUBLISH.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
authors:
  - given-names: "Ivan"
    family-names: "Heredia Jalid"
    email: "ivanjalid@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Córdoba, Argentina"
    # Full URI form. The CFF schema type-checks this field against
    # https://orcid.org/<16 digits>; the bare identifier would fail validation
    # here, and an invalid file silently removes GitHub's "Cite this repository"
    # button. .zenodo.json wants the bare form instead -- see PUBLISH.md 1b.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6702-1295"

repository-code: "https://github.com/ivanjalid1/hsv1-crispr-escape"
url: "https://github.com/ivanjalid1/hsv1-crispr-escape"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
# The date of the v1.0.0 release, in YYYY-MM-DD form. Live now that the release
# exists; it shipped commented out only because the schema type-checks this as a
# date and a placeholder would have invalidated the whole file.
date-released: 2026-09-08

# The Zenodo DOI minted from the release tag. Zenodo reads this file, so this
# field must be the CONCEPT DOI (the one that always resolves to the latest
# version), not the version-specific DOI Zenodo also mints for each release.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22664837"

keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - Cas9
  - SaCas9
  - herpes simplex virus
  - HSV-1
  - guide RNA design
  - sequence conservation
  - viral escape
  - off-target
  - reproducible research

